    "label": "Muffled hearing after a loud gig (example)",
    "review_status": "engineering",
    "digest": "sha256:11160a92102f1cac4a72ea258510748e88279a7597ff2797c0e565ba81a0b788",
    "provenance": "Illustrative temporary threshold shift after loud music, added to normal hearing in both ears: 20-25 dB from 3 to 6 kHz with the peak at 4 kHz, little change below 2 kHz. This is about one standard deviation above the 12.5 dB mean 3-6 kHz shift measured about 9 minutes after concerts in 51 young adults (Murray et al. 2025, doi:10.3389/fauot.2025.1635615), and consistent with concert shifts concentrated around 4 kHz. Calibration matches the other demo presets. Filter workstream example; not audiology-reviewed.",
